        "darwin-arm64",
        "darwin-x64",
        "linux-x64",
        "linux-arm64",
        "win32-x64"
      ],
      "rationale": "📖️ A READER, and that is the whole point of registering it separately from the sibling `quick-xml-svg-1-1-mutate` entry above.\n\nThis subset also carries a `🦀️oracle.rs` that COMPUTES what each mutation should produce. That entry is registered `cross-semio-implementation` and does not discharge anything on its own, because both halves of such a comparison descend from one reading of the specification.\n\nThis entry is a different mechanism. The expected state is not computed at all — it is COMMITTED, as the `after` half of a byte-reproducible fixture built directly by the standalone `quick-xml-svg-codec` binary (`../🏭️generator/🦀️quick-xml-svg-codec`), never by executing this repository's own `SvgMutation`/`SvgDiff` dispatch and never by calling `component.rs`. `quick-xml` 0.42 then parses the element/text/cdata/comment/pi tree on BOTH sides and the comparison is over what it recovered. The probes say so in their own header: \"Everything here MARSHALS and READS; nothing here applies a mutation or predicts what one should.\"\n\nHONESTY SCOPING: `quick-xml` has no notion of SVG semantics — it has never parsed a `viewBox` or `transform` grammar. So unlike `component.rs`'s own decomposed numeric geometry projection (with a float tolerance for cross-implementation formatting noise), this reader's own `svg-1-1-quick-xml-reader-v1` comparisonProfile witnesses `viewBox`/`transform` as OPAQUE ATTRIBUTE STRINGS, exactly like every other attribute. That is still a witnessed, independent comparison — a `viewBox`/`transform` string that changed is caught — it is simply string-level, not semantic. All 9 declared kinds (`set-declaration`, `set-doctype`, `insert-element`, `remove-element`, `set-element-name`, `set-attribute`, `set-text`, `set-view-box`, `set-transform`) are witnessable this way, so none is scoped out with the `-uncarried` convention.\n\nSo the judge is a third-party implementation of generic XML, and nothing in this repository predicts the answer it is judging. That is what makes it qualifying where the sibling entry is not.",
      "comparisonProfiles": [
        "semantic-svg-1-1-v1"
      ]
    }
  ],
